---
# VERITAS C++ formatting. LLVM style, with one deliberate deviation: adjacent
# definition blocks (functions, classes, structs) are always separated by one
# blank line. LLVM's default, `Leave`, silently preserves whatever spacing the
# author happened to leave, which is how src/review ended up with back-to-back
# function definitions.
#
# Keep this file platform-neutral. It is read by `--style=file` from the
# pre-commit hook and must resolve identically on every host.
BasedOnStyle: LLVM
SeparateDefinitionBlocks: Always
...
